<title>USA: USDA hopes for CRP announcement by end of week.</title>
<headline>USDA hopes for CRP announcement by end of week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department hopes to unveil its new Conservation Reserve Program by the end of the week, an aide to Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Asked about CRP by reporters after a signing ceremony to purchase Alaska land, Glickman said, &quot;We're moving as fast as possible. We have nothing to gain from slowing this thing down.&quot;</p>
<p>Glickman said he did not think the Congress's 60-day review period of the regulation was a &quot;real problem.&quot; The aide added that USDA did not think it would apply.</p>
</text>
